  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aawaz II: Inclusion, Accountability and Preventing Modern Slavery - AG - CARE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Care International is the Aawaz II delivery partner in Sindh for the community engagement component of the programme. Establishing the Aawaz Agahi Centres to provide a safe space for transgender persons, people with disabilities, religious minorities, women and girls. The programme will ensure access to state services and to provide information on rights. The partner will convene the community fora (Aawaz District Forums and Aawaz Provincial Forums) for communities to raise demands for services and working together to address social issues including early and forced marriage, child protection, gender-based violence and harmony aong the communities. The programme will establish early warning systems to pre-empt community conflicts to identify and address potential triggers of conflict and promote tolerance.</narrative>
  </description>
